Black Start Manager
Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs.

This product includes software developed by Summon Software Labs.

The Black Start Manager source tree contains no third-party source code. It builds
and tests with a C++20 compiler and CMake alone, with no network access and no
downloaded dependencies. The only non-standard-library interfaces it uses are
operating-system facilities for file creation, file replacement, file locking,
cache flushing, process and socket operations; those are provided by the host
operating system and are not distributed with this repository.

Black Start Manager governs the restart of facility infrastructure from a
de-energized state: restoration sessions, restoration phases, the dependency graph
over restoration obligations, readiness gates, stage entry and exit evidence,
bounded requests to adjacent owners, durable attempt identity, separation of
acknowledgement from observed and verified effect, protected and critical service
prioritization, hold, pause, abort and replan state, authority and generation
binding, stale session fencing, and final return-to-service proof. It does not own
generator, PDU or UPS switching, feed authorization, cooling actuation, network
path recovery, workload startup, incident lifecycle, or vendor building and power
management protocols.

Black Start Manager does not collect or transmit any telemetry. Every record it
writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

